 and quit. Your normal interactive login isn't available to a job started in the background by launchd.\n2. **Why you got no failure note: `status` is a read-only variable in zsh.** In zsh, `status` is just another name for `$?` and can't be assigned to. So the line `status=$?` killed the script before it reached the code that calls `notify.sh`. I confirmed this with `zsh -c 'status=1'`, which fails the same way.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`bin/nightly-review.zsh`:**\n  - Renamed the variable to `rc`.\n  - Added a catch-all that sends a \"FAILED\" message if the script exits with an error for any other reason, so it can't fail silently again.\n  - The failure message now includes the end of the error log, so you see the reason on your phone.\n  - Pre-approved read-only git commands with `--allowedTools`. Without them, the review would hit a new problem once login works: run headless, it can't ask permission to run `git log`.\n  - The script now reads tokens from `~/.config/nightly-review/env` if that file exists.\n- **`bin/notify.sh`:** reads the same env file, so the Telegram token doesn't have to come from the Keychain. You'd only tested it by hand, and the Keychain may be unavailable to a background job at 02:30. It also now exits with an error when Telegram rejects a message, instead of ignoring it.\n\n**What you need to do:** run `claude setup-token` to get a long-lived token. Put `export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=...`, and optionally `TG_BOT_TOKEN`, in `~/.config/nightly-review/env`, then `chmod 600` it. I didn't create any secrets. Then test with `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`; you don't need to reload the plist because it didn't change.\n\n**Testing:** I ran the script locally with a fake `claude` and a fake notifier. The failure, success and missing-repo cases each sent exactly one correct message. I haven't tested a real launchd run, real Claude login or real Telegram delivery.\n\nDetails are in `ANSWER.md`.","ttft_ms":3058,"type":"result"